f the <em>fierceness of the oppressor</em> (? AV) would then be the only use of the word of other than God’s anger; here 𝔊 𝔗 Ew Hi Gf Ke Che Gie RV rightly read <span dir=\"rtl\">חרב</span> <em>oppressing sword</em> (as <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 46:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.46.16\">46:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.16\">50:16</a>). <span dir=\"rtl\">חרון</span> is not used in H P D <sup>2</sup> or E (except song, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 15:7\" href=\"/Exodus.15.7\">Ex 15:7</a>) of the Hex; nor in Ez except <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 7:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.7.12\">7:12</a> (del. Co), v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 7:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.7.14\">14</a>.","note":true}]},"rid":"BDB03446","strong_numbers":["2740"],"next_hw":"חֳרִי","prev_hw":"חָרָה","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["3019"],"TWOT":["736a"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}